/**
 * \page page_custom_backends Writing a Custom Backend
 *
 * ZenitUI is rendering- and windowing-agnostic. To integrate it into a custom
 * engine or a different graphics library (SDL, GLFW + bgfx, Sokol, Vulkan,
 * DirectX, etc.), implement three lightweight interfaces and bind them to
 * `ZenitUI::UIContext`:
 *
 * | Interface | Responsibility |
 * | :--- | :--- |
 * | `IPlatform` | Window size, DPI scale, monotonic clock, pointer/keyboard polling, safe area, clipboard |
 * | `IRenderer` | 2D vector primitives, textures/nine-slice, text metrics & draw, clip/transform/shader stacks, optional off-screen targets  |
 * | `IAssetProvider` | Name-based loading, caching, lookup, and unloading of fonts, textures, and shaders  |
 *
 * All reference classes are grouped under \ref grp_backends.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * \section sec_backend_wiring 1. Wiring a Backend into UIContext
 *
 * Bind your three instances once after creating your window/graphics context,
 * then drive the per-frame cycle inside your main loop:
 *
 * \code{.cpp}
 * MyPlatform      platform;
 * MyRenderer      renderer;
 * MyAssetProvider assets(renderer);
 *
 * auto &ctx = ZenitUI::UIContext::get();
 * ctx.platform = &platform;
 * ctx.renderer = &renderer;
 * ctx.assets   = &assets;
 *
 * // Main loop
 * while (running) {
 *     float dt = computeDeltaTime();
 *     ctx.beginFrame(dt);
 *
 *     root->updateTree(dt);
 *     auto vp = platform.viewportSize();
 *     root->measure(vp.x, vp.y);
 *     root->arrange({0.0f, 0.0f, vp.x, vp.y});
 *
 *     renderer.beginFrame();
 *     root->draw();
 *     renderer.endFrame();
 *
 *     ctx.endFrame();
 * }
 * \endcode
 *
 * ---
 *
 * \section sec_backend_minimum 2. Minimum Viable Backend vs Optional Features
 *
 * You do **not** need shaders or off-screen framebuffers to get a complete UI
 * running. `IRenderer::supports(Feature)` lets a backend opt into advanced
 * capabilities incrementally:
 *
 * - **`Feature::Effects`**: fragment shaders (`pushEffect`, `popEffect`, `setEffect*`).
 * - **`Feature::NestedTargets`**: off-screen render targets for post-processing filters (`createTarget`, `pushTarget`, `popTarget`, `drawTarget`).
 * - **`Feature::TargetSubRect`**: sub-rectangle blitting from pooled render targets.
 *
 * Returning `false` from `supports()` causes ZenitUI to skip shader/filter passes
 * gracefully while keeping layout, widgets, animations, and clipping functional.
 * Start from \ref ZenitUI::Test::MockRenderer to see the smallest valid skeleton,
 * then consult \ref ZenitUI::RaylibRenderer for a full GPU implementation.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * \section sec_backend_invariants 3. Critical Behavioral Invariants
 *
 * Keep these rules in mind when porting to avoid subtle layout or rendering bugs:
 *
 * 1. **Logical vs physical coordinates (`IPlatform` & `IRenderer`)**:
 *    `viewportSize()`, `pointer().pos`, layout rects, and `measureText()` all
 *    operate in **logical pixels**. Apply `dpiScale()` only when configuring the
 *    GPU transform/scissor or sampling the physical framebuffer.
 * 2. **Edge-triggered input (`IPlatform`)**:
 *    `ButtonState::pressed`, `ButtonState::released`, `PointerState::wheelY`,
 *    `InputEvents::keys`, and `InputEvents::chars` must fire for **one frame only**,
 *    whereas `ButtonState::down` and `InputEvents::held` remain true while held.
 * 3. **Intersected clip stack (`IRenderer`)**:
 *    `pushClip(r)` must transform `r` through the active transform stack,
 *    intersect it with the current clip rectangle, and expose the resulting
 *    screen-space clip via `getClipRect()` so off-screen culling stays accurate.
 * 4. **CSS border-box strokes (`IRenderer`)**:
 *    `strokeRect()` and `strokeRoundedRect()` should draw strictly **inside**
 *    the target rectangle so borders sit flush against `fillRect()` /
 *    `fillRoundedRect()` without anti-aliasing gaps.
 * 5. **Zero-allocation asset lookup (`IAssetProvider`)**:
 *    `getFont()`, `getTexture()`, and `getEffect()` are called during layout and
 *    draw; prefer transparent `std::string_view` map lookups (see
 *    `detail::TransparentStringHash` in `RaylibBackend.hpp`).
 * 6. **Safe GPU shutdown**:
 *    If your renderer owns native handles, ensure GPU resources are released
 *    before the graphics context is destroyed (or release them explicitly on
 *    teardown rather than assuming the context is still alive at destructor time).
 *
 * ---
 *
 * \section sec_backend_refs 4. Built-in Reference Implementations
 *
 * Every backend shipped under `backends/` is indexed automatically with its
 * CMake target, supported optional features, and class references:
 *
 * - \subpage page_available_backends "Available Backends" — full auto-generated catalog of all built-in backends.
 * - \ref grp_backends — complete module API reference.
 */